invariant: INV-16
file: x25519_wide_edwards.h
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: select_entry loads the one entry its digit names, so the address
  of the load is the digit's size, three bits of the private key, and the
  cache line it touched says which. The values are right for every digit
  but zero, which the identity below the read covers, so the vectors, the
  equivalence binary and the time all pass. The Semgrep rule
  inv-16-x25519-wide-no-subscript-by-digit refuses the subscript.

--- old
            word_pair entry_low = {row[j][element][0], row[j][element][1]};
--- new
            word_pair entry_low = {row[(size + 7) & 7][element][0], row[(size + 7) & 7][element][1]};
